From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dilip Dalton <dilipdalton@hotmail.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 23:41:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] bdev: lvol and raid bdevs report a volatile write cache

Since v26.09 (7daf05559) the nvmf target advertises the NVMe Volatile
Write Cache only when a namespace bdev reports write_cache. An lvol
bdev never set it and a raid hard-codes 0, so a host of an nvmf export
of either sees no VWC, runs the device write-through and never sends
FLUSH; the lvol FLUSH handler (0002, which commits the blob's
metadata) is then never reached on that path. v26.05 advertised VWC on
every controller, so this keeps what Flint relied on.

An lvol now reports write_cache = 1: with 0002 it holds volatile state
(unsynced blob metadata) that a FLUSH commits. A raid reports it when
any base does, derived in raid_bdev_configure() once the bases are
present; a base added later does not change it (every Flint leg is an
lvol, local or nvmf-attached). bdev_raid_ut gets a
spdk_bdev_has_write_cache() stub; its bases report no cache, so its
write_cache == 0 assertion still holds.

Flint-only; needed from v26.09.

Formerly spdk-csi-driver/docs/spdk-2609-upgrade/write-cache-advertise.patch
(the 2026-09-27 assessment's draft, never applied).
---
 module/bdev/lvol/vbdev_lvol.c                   |  8 ++++++++
 module/bdev/raid/bdev_raid.c                    | 17 +++++++++++++++++
 .../lib/bdev/raid/bdev_raid.c/bdev_raid_ut.c    |  9 +++++++++
 3 files changed, 34 insertions(+)

diff --git a/module/bdev/lvol/vbdev_lvol.c b/module/bdev/lvol/vbdev_lvol.c
index 123c390f2..4cd6b1833 100644
--- a/module/bdev/lvol/vbdev_lvol.c
+++ b/module/bdev/lvol/vbdev_lvol.c
@@ -1259,6 +1259,14 @@ _create_lvol_disk(struct spdk_lvol *lvol, bool destroy)
 	bdev->name = lvol->unique_id;
 	bdev->product_name = "Logical Volume";
 	bdev->blocklen = spdk_bs_get_io_unit_size(lvol->lvol_store->blobstore);
+	/*
+	 * flint: with the lvol FLUSH -> spdk_blob_sync_md handler (lvol-flush-sync.patch)
+	 * an lvol holds volatile state (unsynced blob metadata) that a FLUSH commits. Since
+	 * SPDK v26.09 the nvmf target advertises the NVMe Volatile Write Cache only when a
+	 * namespace's bdev reports write_cache, and a host that sees no VWC never sends
+	 * FLUSH. Report the cache so FLUSH keeps reaching the lvol.
+	 */
+	bdev->write_cache = 1;
 	total_size = spdk_blob_get_num_clusters(lvol->blob) *
 		     spdk_bs_get_cluster_size(lvol->lvol_store->blobstore);
 	assert((total_size % bdev->blocklen) == 0);
diff --git a/module/bdev/raid/bdev_raid.c b/module/bdev/raid/bdev_raid.c
index 48694e1ab..a2d322778 100644
--- a/module/bdev/raid/bdev_raid.c
+++ b/module/bdev/raid/bdev_raid.c
@@ -1961,12 +1961,29 @@ static int
 raid_bdev_configure(struct raid_bdev *raid_bdev, raid_bdev_action_cb cb, void *cb_ctx)
 {
 	uint32_t data_block_size = spdk_bdev_get_data_block_size(&raid_bdev->bdev);
+	struct raid_base_bdev_info *base_info;
 	int rc;
 
 	assert(raid_bdev->state == SPDK_BDEV_RAID_STATE_CONFIGURING);
 	assert(raid_bdev->num_base_bdevs_discovered == raid_bdev->num_base_bdevs_operational);
 	assert(raid_bdev->bdev.blocklen > 0);
 
+	/*
+	 * flint: a raid holds volatile state if any base bdev does. Upstream hard-codes
+	 * write_cache = 0 at creation (raid_bdev_create); since SPDK v26.09 an nvmf
+	 * subsystem exporting such a raid advertises no Volatile Write Cache, hosts then
+	 * never send FLUSH, and the raid's FLUSH fan-out to its bases never runs. Derive
+	 * it from the bases now that they are all present. A base hot-added later does
+	 * not change it: every flint leg is an lvol or an nvmf-attached lvol, all alike.
+	 */
+	RAID_FOR_EACH_BASE_BDEV(raid_bdev, base_info) {
+		if (base_info->desc != NULL &&
+		    spdk_bdev_has_write_cache(spdk_bdev_desc_get_bdev(base_info->desc))) {
+			raid_bdev->bdev.write_cache = 1;
+			break;
+		}
+	}
+
 	/* The strip_size_kb is read in from user in KB. Convert to blocks here for
 	 * internal use.
 	 */
diff --git a/test/unit/lib/bdev/raid/bdev_raid.c/bdev_raid_ut.c b/test/unit/lib/bdev/raid/bdev_raid.c/bdev_raid_ut.c
index effecf2f7..f2453dc93 100644
--- a/test/unit/lib/bdev/raid/bdev_raid.c/bdev_raid_ut.c
+++ b/test/unit/lib/bdev/raid/bdev_raid.c/bdev_raid_ut.c
@@ -141,6 +141,15 @@ static struct raid_bdev_module g_ut_raid_module = {
 };
 RAID_MODULE_REGISTER(&g_ut_raid_module)
 
+/* flint write-cache-advertise.patch: raid_bdev_configure() derives the raid's
+ * write_cache from its bases; the ut's base bdevs report none, so the existing
+ * `write_cache == 0` assertion still holds. */
+bool
+spdk_bdev_has_write_cache(const struct spdk_bdev *bdev)
+{
+	return bdev->write_cache;
+}
+
 DEFINE_STUB_V(spdk_bdev_module_examine_done, (struct spdk_bdev_module *module));
 DEFINE_STUB_V(spdk_bdev_module_list_add, (struct spdk_bdev_module *bdev_module));
 DEFINE_STUB(spdk_bdev_io_type_supported, bool, (struct spdk_bdev *bdev,
